  "method_notes": [
    "Only the four supplied study files informed this analysis. All participants, service and target profiles are fictional; estimates do not describe real UK prevalence.",
    "Analysis tables are embedded under analysis_claims; evidence_refs are exact paths within this JSON. Stable analysis_id values identify raw-data calculations.",
    "Base arrays report unweighted N, sum of supplied weights and Kish ESS. Weighted N is a normalised sample total, not a population count; ESS diagnoses weight concentration.",
    "Each primary endpoint uses its own valid pre/post pair set and preserves random assignment. Consideration top-two is codes 4\u20135 among valid codes 1\u20135, without awareness routing. Numeric 97/98/99 and structural blanks never enter outcome denominators or become zero.",
    "For each arm, D=post-pre; mu=sum(wD)/sum(w); V=[n/(n-1)]sum[w\u00b2(D-mu)\u00b2]/sum(w)\u00b2. Assignment SE uses sqrt(V1+V0); interaction SE sums all four cell variances. Two-sided normal tests and pointwise 95% intervals use the declared policy. No degenerate variance occurred.",
    "Holm adjustment retains three tests in PRIMARY_ASSIGNMENT and separately three interactions in SECONDARY_CHILDREN_HETEROGENEITY. Intervals are not simultaneous; separate families do not provide combined-family .05 error control.",
    "Wave distributions use independent valid cases; primary change uses paired bases. Five-category consideration distributions are retained for both. Rounded percentages may not sum to exactly 100; contrasts were calculated before rounding.",
    "Comparisons with constituent valid N below 40 are suppressed; N below 75 or ESS below 50 requires warning. Reported substantive comparisons clear these thresholds; the exploratory older-online-confident contrast is suppressed.",
    "Diagnostic correlations use pairwise-complete weighted Pearson correlations of coded 1\u20135 responses, without significance searches. Usage-days zero is retained as valid among four-week users.",
    "Inference treats baseline profile weights as fixed and does not account for target-profile uncertainty or repair nonresponse selection. No imputation, attrition adjustment, causal receipt model, mediation claim or post-assignment conditioning was used for the primary estimates."
  ]
